{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please","id":1226884,"title":"More Crunch, Less Fluff Please","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-12T12:31:53-07:00","id":1226884,"title":"More Crunch, Less Fluff Please","content":"In my opinion, many of the Onyx Path books have too much fluff and too little crunch. Would it be possible to release a book that is a compilation of all the crunchy rules bits (merits, powers, etc) with the fluff excluded? I would buy such a book for sure. Am I alone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T12:56:15-07:00","id":1226896,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker is pretty much the closest we've gotten recently. Some books will be more crunch heavy, others will be more lore heavy. Personally, I love both but the lore is what makes CofD books worth spending my money on. The Requiem Clanbooks are fan-favorites and those were almost entirely lore rather than mechanics.<br /> <br /> <b>PS</b>: I have some hangups around the word fluff to mean setting. I know that's not your intent, so I'm not going to derail the thread, but Paizo's James Jacobs <a href=\"http://paizo.com/threads/rzs2l7ns&amp;page=1324?Ask-James-Jacobs-ALL-your-Questions-Here#66195\" target=\"_blank\">pretty much puts it perfectly in my mind</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:32:03-07:00","id":1226907,"title":"","content":"I quite liked Hurt Locker. I am aware that people really like the clan books. I did not like them. The formatting and fonts made the majority of the books difficult to read, and the stories contained on the various post-it notes were not worth the extra effort (in my opinion.) The appendix of the book, where the crunchy bits were located, comprised approximately 15% of the page count. So, why not sell two versions of the book: The Full Size edition at 100% price, and the Crunch only version at 15% price. <br /> <br /> I have found that the last time there was setting information which I found valuable was about the time of Damnation City and the 1st ed. Covenant books. Since then, I feel that the majority of the pages I have bought were indeed Fluff. (my opinion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:02:07-07:00","id":1226922,"title":"","content":"The clan books were pretty much alone, except for the Horror Recognition Guide and Secrets of the Covenants. Most gamelines didn't have anything like them.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that fluff can be seen as unnecessary or unwanted, but it provides context for every bit of crunch in the game.<br /> <br /> The WoDCodex has a lot of information regarding the mechanics, from there you can decide whether you want a book or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2018, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:25:56-07:00","id":1226933,"title":"","content":"The WodCodex is a great resource, and one that I use. However, Onyx Path does not get paid when I do. I would like a way to pay them for what I use and value, without subsidizing what I do not. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the replies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:27:26-07:00","id":1226935,"title":"","content":"Putting asides the problem that fluff is crunch, the bigger problem is that the reality of the matter is fluff sells. Most people who buy these books will not play them, and even if they do, the odds of them playing all of them is small. RPG books tend to sell better as daydream spaces and open fiction, and fluff facilitates that better than crunch.<br /> <br /> Sure, &quot;crunch&quot; is where the action is, but the fact of the matter is that the &quot;fluff&quot; is more in demand simply because it's used more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T15:32:41-07:00","id":1226959,"title":"","content":"Do you have any numbers to back that? To my knowledge, Onyx Path has not been selling to crunch divorced from fluff. So, there are not sales figures to compare. <br /> <br /> It might cost a little more in the way of page layout to release rules, merits, etc divorced from the setting and fiction, but could potentially lead to more sales. Regardless, we won't know unless they try it. Thanks also for your feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T16:10:02-07:00","id":1226966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1226959#post1226959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any numbers to back that? To my knowledge, Onyx Path has not been selling to crunch divorced from fluff. So, there are not sales figures to compare.<br /> <br /> It might cost a little more in the way of page layout to release rules, merits, etc divorced from the setting and fiction, but could potentially lead to more sales. Regardless, we won't know unless they try it. Thanks also for your feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would involve me being one of five people that I am clearly not-but it's not like it's hard to get anyone to admit to this, or to compare success rates without numbers. It's common industry wisdom, and pretty easy to see when you actually look at it.<br /> <br /> You don't have to look far for this-putting asides the strong bet that I have that you think more about the games than you play them, most conversations around the subject are far more about fluff, and a large part of that conversation is contextless, with a lot of players admitting in the open space to a minimal play time, if any at all.<br /> <br /> Also, on the crunch vs fluff subject, one need not look farther than how settingless material performs versus setting based books-hell, any of the Fate games with a setting outsell Fate period despite the mechanical flexibility of the core, with Dresden Files really blowing it out of the water, and that's just an easy example. GURPS, D20 Products, etc., etc. frequently lose out against stuff that has more fluff than mechanics. An argument can be made over the successes of stuff that is lean-but-still-fluff-based versus those of heavier fluff, particularly since a lot of the heavier fluff stuff also forms a lot of old guard material, but pieces like Numenera indicate the trend I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> A broad view of what's selling, how well, and how the conversations about games are going reinforces those notions, and what commentary we get from people who do handle the numbers supports the notion, and that's before you account just for how pretty much ever long-standing professional I have put the question to has affirmed the idea that fluff is what people respond to financially. If I get different results once I start pushing The Noble &amp; The Sovereign Trilogy, I'll let you know (since those games will be ones I actually would have 'numbers' on).<br /> <br /> None of this is to say that &quot;crunch&quot; isn't important-I got whole new characters for Beast from the BPG based on some of the Atavisms-but a box of crunch doesn't excite and inform the imagination nearly as much fluff does. Using another case in point, I have seen more conversation about Hurt Locker, a still fairly light fluffy supplement, versus Armory, a book entirely about crunch.<br /> <br /> It's a weird reality to fit to, but it is how RPG's are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T18:07:22-07:00","id":1226988,"title":"","content":"I am not an industry insider, so some of this is new information to me. Thanks for sharing. Also, if i have given the impression that I think Onyx Path should stop printing anything other than rules and new merits and such, I apologize. That was not my intention. However, I would still like an opportunity to purchase the crunchy bits separately. They have already been written, and we now use a PDF/PoD business so it's not like they have to take the risk of publishing and stocking thousands of physical books. I suspect even those that love the fluff would consider buying a single tome with all the rules in one place. <br /> <br /> As for whether I spend more time playing in or thinking about the games: I am fortunate in that I have been playing WW/OP games for over 20 years now. I run a game of mage and play a game of vampire every other week. <br /> <br /> Thanks again for your input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T19:28:07-07:00","id":1227016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1226935#post1226935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting asides the problem that fluff is crunch, the bigger problem is that the reality of the matter is fluff sells. Most people who buy these books will not play them, and even if they do, the odds of them playing all of them is small. RPG books tend to sell better as daydream spaces and open fiction, and fluff facilitates that better than crunch.<br /> <br /> Sure, &quot;crunch&quot; is where the action is, but the fact of the matter is that the &quot;fluff&quot; is more in demand simply because it's used more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is anecdotal, so grain of salt, but if I buy a book, I plan to use it. Why would I buy something I'm not going to play? If I decided I was never going to play vampire, I wouldn't purchase VtR and SotC. I just buy an RPG I and my friends would play with the same money.<br /> <br /> That aside, I do agree with the op that OPP books are a little on the fluffy side. There is a time and place for fluff, don't get me wrong- I just wish we could get a few more other bits in instead of the 'slice of life stories' in every chapter- save those for the anthologies. Let me buy that separate, and please don't put it in those weird fonts and colors, because those get hard to read sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T19:46:13-07:00","id":1227018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227016#post1227016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, this is anecdotal, so grain of salt, but if I buy a book, I plan to use it. Why would I buy something I'm not going to play? If I decided I was never going to play vampire, I wouldn't purchase VtR and SotC. I just buy an RPG I and my friends would play with the same money.</div> </div> </div> </div>You already use the book when you read it. It is true that playing with it is using it more, but i think you already can get something out of the book by simply reading it.<br /> <br /> Also, sometimes just the hope that you may someday run or play a game from that book is enough, at least thats what i tell myself. (looks at my copy of Promethean, sigh)<br /> I guess it also depends on the available funds you have. Right now my money is low enough that i've decided to only buy new books if i'm certain i'll play them. But when i'll have more money i'll probably be more loose with buying books that sparks my interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T19:51:38-07:00","id":1227019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227016#post1227016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, this is anecdotal, so grain of salt, but if I buy a book, I plan to use it. Why would I buy something I'm not going to play? If I decided I was never going to play vampire, I wouldn't purchase VtR and SotC. I just buy an RPG I and my friends would play with the same money.<br /> <br /> That aside, I do agree with the op that OPP books are a little on the fluffy side. There is a time and place for fluff, don't get me wrong- I just wish we could get a few more other bits in instead of the 'slice of life stories' in every chapter- save those for the anthologies. Let me buy that separate, and please don't put it in those weird fonts and colors, because those get hard to read sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're gonna get anecdotal, let me counterbalance.<br /> <br /> I also buy books with an expectation to use them. I want to play and run every single line of this game, and every single variation of Golden Sky Stories, and Don't Rest Your Head and Misspent Youth and Chill and Ryuutama and Mouse Guard and Monsterhearts and 5 Acts in Tragedy and Starlit Kingdom and Tenra Basho Zero and<br /> <br /> at some point, I realized that while I <i>intend</i> to, there's <i>no</i> realistic way I will be able to use all of the material on RPG's I get in the way they were intended. I never buy stuff thinking I won't, but I end up not being able too. Any single game I get alone has at least five or six games in them at a minimum. None of that makes it useless, because I still fun exploring these worlds imagining stories and characters for them, and none of that changes my intent-I want to and will work to run as many games and play as many of these games as I can.<br /> <br /> But at some point, my games outrun them, and none of that makes the games less of a waste for me.<br /> <br /> Hell, I live in a household of gamers with the weekends open, coming up on a year of gaming and we still have only gotten around to two games, neither of them being the games on my bucket list.<br /> <br /> Now, using myself as a point of comparison is not where my point here comes from. I thought I was an exception with that, since it seemed to me like a lot of people were much more niche and loyal to their niche than I was a very exploratory type. But then a lot of experts I chatted with, including Matthew McFarland and Olivia Hill, basically laid out the facts as they had seen over the years annnnnd yeah.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of people <i>plan</i> to use them. But unless you manage to actually <i>use</i> all of it, the difference between a plan and a daydream is moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:23:07-07:00","id":1227026,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the anecdotes. <br /> <br /> To my original point though: Would you have a problem if Onyx Path decided to offer some or all of their books such that the rules/merits/powers could be purchased separately at a reduced price, while still offering the full book including all the setting/fiction at full price for those that wanted it? Or even the setting/fiction without the crunch?<br /> <br /> I feel like the thread has become a thread of 'fluff defense.' I am not trying to take away setting/fiction from those that like it. I am just realizing that all (and I do mean all) of the setting/fiction that I have purchased and read from Onyx Path in several years has been, in my opinion: not very good. I have not and will not use any of it in my games.<br /> <br /> What I do like, and what I have always liked most about white-wolf and later onyx path, is their dice system. It is simple to understand and quick to implement at the table. Combat and other tests can be adjudicated quickly without slowing down the story. I love it. So for me, being able to buy the 20 or so pages which are relevant to my gaming experience without having to buy the art and stories I do not care about would be really attractive. Considering the existence of markets like DrivethruRPG, I would think that this would be relatively painless to implement. I would even settle for a barely formatted text file. <br /> <br /> I am not saying 'stop liking what I don't like.' I am asking for an option to purchase what I like about Onyx Path games without subsidizing what I don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:34:34-07:00","id":1227034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227026#post1227026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the anecdotes.<br /> <br /> To my original point though: Would you have a problem if Onyx Path decided to offer some or all of their books such that the rules/merits/powers could be purchased separately at a reduced price, while still offering the full book including all the setting/fiction at full price for those that wanted it? Or even the setting/fiction without the crunch?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't object to it, I just don't think it would provide enough returns to actually warrant the practice. And that actually goes in either direction-pure fluff pieces <i>do</i> suffer from lack of crunch (consider how fiction compilations do seem to undersell, as a minor point).<br /> <br /> But when discussing Fluff vs Crunch, I want people to consider the range between, say, the VtR Clanbooks,the Beast's or Demon's Players Guide, and Hurt Locker the vast approval of all of those (and how that is expressed), and the contrasting amounts of fluff and crunch in those pieces.<br /> <br /> I do want to clarify I get the crunch desire-back in the DnD days, I didn't grab any of the setting books because I felt like the fluff got in the way of me getting to the actual tools for making my own story. I may not run that way anymore, but once upon a time and all that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:36:04-07:00","id":1227035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227026#post1227026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my original point though: Would you have a problem if Onyx Path decided to offer some or all of their books such that the rules/merits/powers could be purchased separately at a reduced price, while still offering the full book including all the setting/fiction at full price for those that wanted it? Or even the setting/fiction without the crunch?<br /> <br /> I feel like the thread has become a thread of 'fluff defense.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sorry about that. I wouldn't have a problem with it, though I don't think it's that wanted, there's a lot of 'fluff' questions in regards to how to run certain things, and once you get into the supernatural, pure mechanics without context is just nonsense, looking at the disciplines and merits alone wouldn't really inform you about the clans or covenants, which are really 'one' with the mechanics, to paraphrase ArcaneArts said, much fluff is crunch. Plus there would be extra work where it comes to editing out all the fluff, which would have to be balanced out by extra sales of this abbreviated copy.<br /> <br /> I have stated on occasion how I'd like a version of the pdf without the graphics, similar to the 99% complete examples we had with Kickstarters, just because it's easier to put onto and read from an eReader. But I don't think it would justify a cheaper price, just something that comes with the full pdf purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2018, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:38:36-07:00","id":1227037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227034#post1227034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't object to it, I just don't think it would provide enough returns to actually warrant the practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the editing and layout time to consider. It isn't nearly as simple as saying &quot;delete all the lore.&quot; You'd have to basically lay out an entire other book.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Ninja'd by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:44:10-07:00","id":1227039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227037#post1227037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is also the editing and layout time to consider. It isn't nearly as simple as saying &quot;delete all the lore.&quot; You'd have to basically lay out an entire other book.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Ninja'd by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And while fluff is harder to write, mechanics tend to be a <i>bitch</i> to layout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T21:46:24-07:00","id":1227044,"title":"","content":"Now, the folks writing and developing for Onyx Path have rotated a bit recently, so this may not be accurate any more, but as of not too long ago, the majority of the devs were of the &quot;there is no 'fluff' and 'crunch,' only game content&quot; camp. Not a defense of one approach or another, just thought you might want to be aware of when looking for a different crunch-to-fluff ratio in OPP products; the folks making those products might not really be thinking about it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T21:51:26-07:00","id":1227045,"title":"","content":"As an aside, <a href=\"https://mythcreants.com/blog/what-writers-can-learn-from-the-roleplaying-concept-of-flavor/\" target=\"_blank\">look, slightly relevant blog from place I visit,</a> I speak good English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T22:56:24-07:00","id":1227053,"title":"","content":"I like flavour being in the books, it informs the mechanics and provides themes and a tone. But.... I'm never going to buy something like Secrets of the Covenants or the Clan Books because of how they're basically just flavour that doesn't engage with me in anyway because of the way it's written, and do hope future books have ratios of Flavour to Mechanics more like the Core books of the lines. If I want to read novels or short stories, I buy a novel or an anthology of short stories, not a RPG supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 06-13-2018, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T23:07:49-07:00","id":1227055,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to second nofather in that if you were ever to strip a CofD book down to <i>just</i> the mechanics I suspect you\u2019d end up with something that doesn\u2019t make enough sense to play. CofD isn\u2019t the kind of system whose flavor is really designed to be modular; on the contrary, the rules are almost always meant to push, pull, and nudge you towards fairly particular types of stories, which means if you don\u2019t know what types of stories those are you\u2019re missing a lot of context to why things work the way they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T23:10:11-07:00","id":1227056,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants is an odd exception for me, because I <i>did</i> buy that for the mechanics and have yet to read any of the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T23:22:36-07:00","id":1227058,"title":"","content":"Thanks Willow for the insight. I can see and understand why a game developer would want to classify everything as 'game content.' I even agree. Everything in the books is game content. However, it seems that as I look at my books there is a pattern. The majority of the book is fiction and setting info, and then there is an appendix comprising approximately 15% of the page count. It is in the appendix where they keep all the goodies like new merits and such. It seems the developers know quite well the difference between crunch and fluff. They even segregate the two in the books. <br /> <br /> As a slight aside: I did just open my pdf of Secrets of the Covenants. I flipped to the Ordo Dracul section in an attempt to find something informative. Instead, there was a narrative of someone essentially performing scales (skin graft) and disciplines (animalism, raise the familiar.) At this point, I think a better terms than crunch and fluff would be signal and noise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T23:30:45-07:00","id":1227059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227058#post1227058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, I think a better terms than crunch and fluff would be signal and noise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure. Noise implies the sound of static to me with connotations of interference and disruption. If we need to label thing, just call them what they are: lore and mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T23:38:46-07:00","id":1227060,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">noun: <b>lore</b></span><ul><li>&quot;a body of traditions and knowledge on a subject or held by a particular group, typically passed from person to person by word of mouth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I will use mechanics and lore where appropriate from now on. However, I do not think the content of Secrets of the Covenants qualifies. Definitely Noise (in my opinion) with the exception of the mechanics in the appendix. Those were great.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T00:29:44-07:00","id":1227067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227058#post1227058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Willow for the insight. I can see and understand why a game developer would want to classify everything as 'game content.' I even agree. Everything in the books is game content.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227058#post1227058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it seems that as I look at my books there is a pattern. The majority of the book is fiction and setting info, and then there is an appendix comprising approximately 15% of the page count. It is in the appendix where they keep all the goodies like new merits and such. It seems the developers know quite well the difference between crunch and fluff. They even segregate the two in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you really call a five book series published a decade ago for the previous edition of the game and one book from the current edition that\u2019s an intentional throwback to that series a pattern though? Especially when that five book series was only an eighth of the previous edition\u2019s catalogue?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227058#post1227058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a slight aside: I did just open my pdf of Secrets of the Covenants. I flipped to the Ordo Dracul section in an attempt to find something informative. Instead, there was a narrative of someone essentially performing scales (skin graft) and disciplines (animalism, raise the familiar.) At this point, I think a better terms than crunch and fluff would be signal and noise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it any wonder that the thread quickly turns into a defense of non-mechanical content when your correction of the widely controversial fluff/crunch model is to switch to an even more derisive new dichotomy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T00:30:34-07:00","id":1227068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227056#post1227056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secrets of the Covenants is an odd exception for me, because I <i>did</i> buy that for the mechanics and have yet to read any of the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T00:39:53-07:00","id":1227074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227055#post1227055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m going to second nofather in that if you were ever to strip a CofD book down to <i>just</i> the mechanics I suspect you\u2019d end up with something that doesn\u2019t make enough sense to play. CofD isn\u2019t the kind of system whose flavor is really designed to be modular; on the contrary, the rules are almost always meant to push, pull, and nudge you towards fairly particular types of stories, which means if you don\u2019t know what types of stories those are you\u2019re missing a lot of context to why things work the way they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they <i>tried</i> for modular flavor early in CofD\u2019s (read: \u201cNWoD\u2019s\u201d) lifespan, hence the commonly-cited \u201ctoolbox\u201d nature of the setting. But I agree with you. CofD is at its strongest when its fluff and crunch are married closest; when the mechanics reinforce the lore to create a game with a cohesive tone and a consistent message. In that sense, I agree with figurehead. A book of 85% story content and 15% rules content and a stark division between the two is not a strong CofD product. But I don\u2019t think the solution is to sell that 15% separately as a discount. I think the solution is to integrate the mechanics more directly into the rest of the book. If that 15% was more intimately related to the other 85, it wouldn\u2019t be nearly so frustrating that it\u2019s such a small portion of the book. IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T01:07:37-07:00","id":1227076,"title":"","content":"The non-derisive way to discuss it is mechanics and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T06:15:37-07:00","id":1227123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227026#post1227026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the anecdotes. <br /> <br /> To my original point though: Would you have a problem if Onyx Path decided to offer some or all of their books such that the rules/merits/powers could be purchased separately at a reduced price, while still offering the full book including all the setting/fiction at full price for those that wanted it? Or even the setting/fiction without the crunch?<br /> <br /> I feel like the thread has become a thread of 'fluff defense.' I am not trying to take away setting/fiction from those that like it. I am just realizing that all (and I do mean all) of the setting/fiction that I have purchased and read from Onyx Path in several years has been, in my opinion: not very good. I have not and will not use any of it in my games.<br /> <br /> What I do like, and what I have always liked most about white-wolf and later onyx path, is their dice system. It is simple to understand and quick to implement at the table. Combat and other tests can be adjudicated quickly without slowing down the story. I love it. So for me, being able to buy the 20 or so pages which are relevant to my gaming experience without having to buy the art and stories I do not care about would be really attractive. Considering the existence of markets like DrivethruRPG, I would think that this would be relatively painless to implement. I would even settle for a barely formatted text file. <br /> <br /> I am not saying 'stop liking what I don't like.' I am asking for an option to purchase what I like about Onyx Path games without subsidizing what I don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see doing a sort of DM screen and quick reference book or rule codex with source references. That'd be really nice honestly, because trying to dig through everything to find a mechanic can be annoying.<br /> <br /> I've actually had players who have that specific problem- digging through all the fluff to figure out the depths of the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T08:59:46-07:00","id":1227155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227076#post1227076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The non-derisive way to discuss it is mechanics and setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I prefer to think of it has 'the game' and 'subsystems'.<br /> <br /> Most of the content is a description of the game: here's the world, here's what you play in it, here are things you can encounter, here's what happens to you when you do encounter them.<br /> <br /> Then there is the subsystems: When encountering something as described above, you can use this math to resolve what happens if it is non-obvious or you just want to leave it up to chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T10:21:12-07:00","id":1227169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227155#post1227155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer to think of it has 'the game' and 'subsystems'.<br /> <br /> Most of the content is a description of the game: here's the world, here's what you play in it, here are things you can encounter, here's what happens to you when you do encounter them.<br /> <br /> Then there is the subsystems: When encountering something as described above, you can use this math to resolve what happens if it is non-obvious or you just want to leave it up to chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not all rules content is subsystems. Combat is a system and called shots are a subsystem, but the Martial Arts Fighting Style is just a rules element that interacts with the combat system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T11:52:01-07:00","id":1227190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227169#post1227169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But not all rules content is subsystems. Combat is a system and called shots are a subsystem, but the Martial Arts Fighting Style is just a rules element that interacts with the combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, really I should have said 'systems' in the first place not 'subsystems', that was needlessly specific of me. So Systems in general would include the basic rules for a system, any subsystem,or any other rule that interfaces with that system in a specific manner.<br /> <br /> I would also say that for me, content like Merits (or Discplines, Gifts, etc) are more generalized than that. Some portions of it are a description of its effect in a general sense, this is no different then the description of what a Ventrue is, then other parts interact with systems (the Dot rating and prerequisites are connected to the Merits system, the effects on combat part of the combat system, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T12:38:44-07:00","id":1227197,"title":"","content":"1. Fluff and Crunch are the most commonly used and commonly understood words describe the dichotomy of game content. They are not 'widely controversial.' Even the people in this thread who do not like those words cannot agree on what to use instead. setting/fiction/lore/mechanics/systems/sub-systems/game content? I'm not going to play the semantics game.<br /> <br /> 2. There haven't even been many releases per game line since 2nd Edition. I think in Vampire that has been, the Core Book +3? So, 5 books from 1st ed and 1/3 supplements from 2nd is a pretty strong pattern. I referenced those books because they are the worst examples of fluff I would rather not pay for, while still containing some of the best crunch in the back of the book. They were referenced in counterpoint to those who made the point that fluff and crunch are inseparable. <br /> <br /> 3. I will concede that separating the fluff from the crunch in the Core books is not a great idea. However, with regard to the supplements that is not the case. Readers of the core book absolutely have enough context to use the crunch introduced in the pages of supplements. <br /> <br /> 4. I'm glad to hear they are rotating the writers and am looking forward to see what the new team will do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T14:13:40-07:00","id":1227227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227197#post1227197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. I will concede that separating the fluff from the crunch in the Core books is not a great idea. However, with regard to the supplements that is not the case. Readers of the core book absolutely have enough context to use the crunch introduced in the pages of supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pop quiz: What are the Obcasus Rites and how do they work? What are Heralds and how do they work?<br /> <br /> Supplements often introduce elements that are sideways to expectations and require context to fully accept and use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T14:31:54-07:00","id":1227236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227197#post1227197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Fluff and Crunch are the most commonly used and commonly understood words describe the dichotomy of game content. They are not 'widely controversial.' Even the people in this thread who do not like those words cannot agree on what to use instead. setting/fiction/lore/mechanics/systems/sub-systems/game content? I'm not going to play the semantics game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do as you will, but if you call it fluff and crunch, don\u2019t be surprised when the conversation gets derailed by defense of story content and arguments for terms it might be better to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227197#post1227197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. There haven't even been many releases per game line since 2nd Edition. I think in Vampire that has been, the Core Book +3? So, 5 books from 1st ed and 1/3 supplements from 2nd is a pretty strong pattern. I referenced those books because they are the worst examples of fluff I would rather not pay for, while still containing some of the best crunch in the back of the book. They were referenced in counterpoint to those who made the point that fluff and crunch are inseparable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was the person you were referencing them in counter-point to, and I did not say fluff and crunch are inseparable. I said that most of the folks at Onyx Path as of recently prefer to think of all content as game content. At any rate, one example does not make a pattern, no matter how small your sample size is. There is one 2e book that used the format of the Clan books, and it was an intentional callback to them. That\u2019s not a pattern, unless you <i>really</i> stretch the definition of the word. It wasn\u2019t a pattern in 1e either, it was one eighth of Requiem\u2019s catalogue and they all came out within a year of each other. That\u2019s not a pattern either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227197#post1227197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I will concede that separating the fluff from the crunch in the Core books is not a great idea. However, with regard to the supplements that is not the case. Readers of the core book absolutely have enough context to use the crunch introduced in the pages of supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don\u2019t think that would play to the game\u2019s strengths, nor would it sell well with the game\u2019s core audiences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227197#post1227197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. I'm glad to hear they are rotating the writers and am looking forward to see what the new team will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s... not what I meant. A couple of the developers who played a big role in early 2e have moved on to other things. It\u2019s not like they\u2019re consciously rotating people in and out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T14:54:48-07:00","id":1227241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227236#post1227236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do as you will, but if you call it fluff and crunch, don\u2019t be surprised when the conversation gets derailed by defense of story content and arguments for terms it might be better to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be somewhat rude to clutter up a thread with unrelated topics. It actually might not be a bad idea for an enterprising soul to go ahead and make a separate thread for that. I'm still honestly a little curious what folks are offended by in those terms- I seem to have missed that memo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227236#post1227236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don\u2019t think that would play to the game\u2019s strengths, nor would it sell well with the game\u2019s core audiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about the marketing of OPP and the games or their target audience. I know that to get the players I know and normally play with to play a CoD game, I have to create sheets of rules to hand out because none of us really want to go through the anthologies or story stuff written into the books. We need to know names, basics about what those names mean, the bare bones of the setting, and then we can work from there on our own.<br /> <br /> I suppose in a way, my group is more like board game players- we need the core mechanics, and we can have fun with that, without any of the pre-written narratives or most of setting information- we don't even normally get into the political aspects of the game very much normally. A few basics are all we really need in that realm. I mean, we already sold anthologies that are exactly what one crowd wants. Why not give the other team, so to speak, a rules compendium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:01:55-07:00","id":1227245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227241#post1227241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about the marketing of OPP and the games or their target audience. I know that to get the players I know and normally play with to play a CoD game, I have to create sheets of rules to hand out because none of us really want to go through the anthologies or story stuff written into the books. We need to know names, basics about what those names mean, the bare bones of the setting, and then we can work from there on our own.</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't exactly being forced to read anthologies, or even 'story stuff.' In both the clanbooks and Secrets of the Covenants, all the mechanics are in one spot, the back of the book. It's actually a trend they've been doing in Dark Eras and Night Horrors (since the first), where you have a write-up of an antagonist or setting, then the setting relevant mechanics or the antagonists stats or new abilities in the back of that section. Most of the second edition books have tables of contents that let you know where certain rules are, and they tend to be in chunks with other rules. Skipping to the rules section is easier than ever, but these rules play off of the setting.<br /> <br /> The only actual fiction anthology that also contained mechanics, Interface, also separated those in their own sections after the relevant fiction. But in some cases, for instance the core books or player's guides, mechanics can't be completely separate from the setting. Some people might just want to know what sacred hunt blessing a lodge offers, but without the context of what the lodge is about, it's just mechanical nonsense.<br /> <br /> What books are you and your players having trouble with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-13-2018, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:02:37-07:00","id":1227246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227241#post1227241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be somewhat rude to clutter up a thread with unrelated topics. It actually might not be a bad idea for an enterprising soul to go ahead and make a separate thread for that. I'm still honestly a little curious what folks are offended by in those terms- I seem to have missed that memo.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> already posted a link to, here is an example: <a href=\"http://paizo.com/threads/rzs2l7ns&amp;page=1324?Ask-James-Jacobs-ALL-your-Questions-Here#66195\" target=\"_blank\">http://paizo.com/threads/rzs2l7ns&amp;pa...ons-Here#66195</a><br /> <br /> TLDR: 'Fluff' implies that it is not important, that it is only padding at best. The connection to the pornography industry only makes it worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:19:54-07:00","id":1227249,"title":"","content":"Customer: \u201cHi there, I noticed you have \u2018Surf and Turf\u2019 on the menu. I\u2019ve eaten here before and I didn\u2019t care for the seafood. Can I just buy the steak?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cWe do not serve \u2018Surf and Turf.\u2019 Those terms are offensive.\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cThere is no \u2018Surf and Turf,\u2019 only dinner.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cWell, can\u2019t you put the part of dinner that is not from the sea on a plate by itself and sell it to me?\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cOur lobster is amazing. You won\u2019t even know what to do with the steak if the lobster is not on the plate with it.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak. You already have steaks and plates right?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cIt would take too much time for the expediter to arrange the filet properly on a plate without the lobster to balance it out.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak, seafood is expensive. Can\u2019t I just pay for what I am going to eat?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou heard the chef. You wouldn\u2019t even know what to do with the filet without the lobster.\u201d<br /> Customer:\u201dCan I just get a yes or no answer to my question?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou really should have expected this after using such offensive language.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:28:02-07:00","id":1227250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227249#post1227249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customer:\u201dCan I just get a yes or no answer to my question?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>You got a yes or no answer to your question and this tortured analogy is not going to get you a &quot;yes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:28:18-07:00","id":1227251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227249#post1227249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customer: \u201cHi there, I noticed you have \u2018Surf and Turf\u2019 on the menu. I\u2019ve eaten here before and I didn\u2019t care for the seafood. Can I just buy the steak?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cWe do not serve \u2018Surf and Turf.\u2019 Those terms are offensive.\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cThere is no \u2018Surf and Turf,\u2019 only dinner.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cWell, can\u2019t you put the part of dinner that is not from the sea on a plate by itself and sell it to me?\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cOur lobster is amazing. You won\u2019t even know what to do with the steak if the lobster is not on the plate with it.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak. You already have steaks and plates right?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cIt would take too much time for the expediter to arrange the filet properly on a plate without the lobster to balance it out.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak, seafood is expensive. Can\u2019t I just pay for what I am going to eat?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou heard the chef. You wouldn\u2019t even know what to do with the filet without the lobster.\u201d<br /> Customer:\u201dCan I just get a yes or no answer to my question?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou really should have expected this after using such offensive language.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a pretty bad comparison, aside from being reductive it is inaccurate. I tried to think of an accurate example also using food but it is too reductive for me to do so. Comparing the intention of writing a game as a combination of descriptive and descriptive (mechanics) elements to any combination of physical products is just absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:46:58-07:00","id":1227255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227249#post1227249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customer: \u201cHi there, I noticed you have \u2018Surf and Turf\u2019 on the menu. I\u2019ve eaten here before and I didn\u2019t care for the seafood. Can I just buy the steak?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cWe do not serve \u2018Surf and Turf.\u2019 Those terms are offensive.\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cThere is no \u2018Surf and Turf,\u2019 only dinner.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cWell, can\u2019t you put the part of dinner that is not from the sea on a plate by itself and sell it to me?\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cOur lobster is amazing. You won\u2019t even know what to do with the steak if the lobster is not on the plate with it.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak. You already have steaks and plates right?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cIt would take too much time for the expediter to arrange the filet properly on a plate without the lobster to balance it out.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak, seafood is expensive. Can\u2019t I just pay for what I am going to eat?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou heard the chef. You wouldn\u2019t even know what to do with the filet without the lobster.\u201d<br /> Customer:\u201dCan I just get a yes or no answer to my question?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou really should have expected this after using such offensive language.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is more akin to cooking a steak by seasoning it, deciding whether the grill(or pan) should be coated in butter, lard, vegetable oil or olive oil, what sort of vegetables you want to go with it, and what wine or liquor you want to pair it with....and just serving a steak you left on a hot pan for a set amount of time.<br /> <br /> Outside of setting-agnostic* games like GURPS, mechanics emerge from the setting and are the way they are because they express the reality of their context. To sever them from that context and expect it to be as rewarding as with it is...a strange notion.<br /> <br /> I mean, I dunno, maybe you like GURPS, but if that's the case, why would we need anything other than the Chronicles of Darkness book?<br /> <br /> Again, Fluff is kind of the point for a large part of the audience, and when that's the way it goes, it becomes clear why that word is loaded.<br /> <br /> *This is a weird term when you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-13-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:17:28-07:00","id":1227264,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> @ArcaneArts: I haven't read Beast (googled Obcasus Rites.) I have, however read most of the Requiem Books. Cover to cover. Many of them I found very useful. VtRcore, Covenant Books and Damnation city would be my top picks. My point is this: After reading all this content from this company I feel that most of of it is not of high quality and not worth the money spent on page count. The merits, disciplines, conditions and the like (crunch, if you will) is of very high quality and very much worth the money spent on page count. I do appreciate your willingness to chat and your yes/no answer.<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin: I did not give 1 example. I gave 6. Secrets of the Covenants + 5 clan books. I have similar feelings about the various bloodlines books (4 more examples) wherein new merits/disciplines/devotions are mixed in with stuff I did not like and will not use. The bloodlines books aren't as bad as the clanbooks because they are printed in plain easy to read fonts.<br /> <br /> @ElvesofZion: There are many words in the english language that have multiple means/connotations. Often positive, negative, and neutral meanings and uses of the same word exist. Here are some examples: wicked, sick, dick, basic, and of course fluff. In the specific case of fluff, It has been used commonly in the Table Top RPG hobby in a neutral sense for decades. Being offended by its use is a choice. <br /> <br /> @nofather: It is true no one is being forced to buy/read the fiction anthologies. However, they exist for those that want them. No such option exists for those that would like a rules compendium.<br /> <br /> @Satchel: I have gotten a yes/no from one person. Perhaps others would like to give theirs. (ie: Yes, I would like the opportunity to buy book which is comprised exclusively of the disciplines/merits/conditions without any of the fiction or setting attached. or No, I would not like that opportunity.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Once again: No one is saying OP should stop writing and publishing books in the style they have been. I am asking for an additional book to published every once in awhile which compiles all the new merits/disciplines/conditions/etc which have been created.<br /> <br /> For example: I love the work of author Jim Butcher. He often contributes to short story anthologies. Well, I do not wish to buy the other stories in the anthology. Lucky for me, every once in a while the various short stories Mr. Butcher has written get compiled into one book. 'Side Jobs' and 'Brief Cases' are two such books. I get to buy/read the stories I want, and leave those I don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:21:20-07:00","id":1227265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227255#post1227255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also, given the way things work in a setting-first system, it would actually be more accurate to describe the mechanics as the seasoning, sides, and drink. Which makes sense given the argument I'm making.</div> </div> </div> </div>This analogy I can get on board with. Give me my seasoning and let me go sprinkle it on some chicken, without having to buy a steak, as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:35:16-07:00","id":1227269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227265#post1227265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This analogy I can get on board with. Give me my seasoning and let me go sprinkle it on some chicken, without having to buy a steak, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, that does expose the flaw of looking at it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:55:00-07:00","id":1227271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227265#post1227265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This analogy I can get on board with. Give me my seasoning and let me go sprinkle it on some chicken, without having to buy a steak, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I concur. And as I mentioned before, I'd be 100% onboard with with a just mechanics book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T17:13:23-07:00","id":1227274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227265#post1227265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This analogy I can get on board with. Give me my seasoning and let me go sprinkle it on some chicken, without having to buy a steak, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this extension of the analogy the chicken is\u2026 what, exactly?<br /> <br /> You've pretty much just spoken in the abstract \u2014 and derisively so, at points \u2014 to a vague supposition that the setting and the mechanics being written to directly inform each other is just sort of a lazy lie that you've been told to keep you from getting &quot;just the mechanics,&quot; so I <i>assume</i> you are not counting, say, Mage 2e's setting-chapter breakdown of what the Lex Magica is as a totally separate thing from the mage-specific-rules-chapter blurb of what the Lex Megica Merit does, or that Demon's supplementary expansion of Infrastructure hacking holds the same degree of meaning without the framing of how Infrastructure works and what it is, but at that point the necessary definition of &quot;fluff&quot; you're leaning on is &quot;the chapter fiction and the sample settings,&quot; not anything remotely approaching eighty-five percent of the book's content.<br /> <br /> If that assumption is a faulty one, then the thing you are looking for is nothing so ridiculously-stated as a mechanical equivalent of the fiction anthologies.<br /> <br /> If that assumption is a faulty one, then the thing you are looking for is a <i>whole-system </i><i>quick-reference document</i>.<br /> <br /> That is a very different thing and much more inoffensive in scope even if it is also something that can be managed with index cards or college-lined cheat-sheets for less investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T17:28:46-07:00","id":1227280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227264#post1227264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin: I did not give 1 example. I gave 6. Secrets of the Covenants + 5 clan books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely ignoring the context those books exist in. The 5 clan books were a series, whose style was an intentional departure from their standard style. They were also a very small portion of the 1e catalogue. They do not represent a pattern. Secrets of the Covenants was from a different edition of the game than the 5 clan books were, and was an intentional throwback to the style that the clan book series was written in. It also does not represent a pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227264#post1227264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have similar feelings about the various bloodlines books (4 more examples) wherein new merits/disciplines/devotions are mixed in with stuff I did not like and will not use. The bloodlines books aren't as bad as the clanbooks because they are printed in plain easy to read fonts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the clan books were not 85% &quot;fluff&quot; with a 15% &quot;crunch&quot; appendix, which is what you claimed the pattern you were noticing looked like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T17:42:48-07:00","id":1227285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227249#post1227249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customer: \u201cHi there, I noticed you have \u2018Surf and Turf\u2019 on the menu. I\u2019ve eaten here before and I didn\u2019t care for the seafood. Can I just buy the steak?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cWe do not serve \u2018Surf and Turf.\u2019 Those terms are offensive.\u201d<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Waiter: \u201cYou really should have expected this after using such offensive language.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason this sounds absurd is because you've distanced your analogy from the context of the discussion. &quot;fluff&quot; and &quot;crunch&quot; are loaded terms that carry implications about the value of the content they describe. &quot;seafood&quot; and &quot;steak&quot; are not. A more apt analogy would be if you asked for just the meal without the bottom-feeder. And if instead of asking the waiter, you were asking other customers. If you did that, it would be pretty natural to expect those other customers to respond that they think the lobster is a primary feature of surf and turf, and to ask you not to imply that steak is a meal while lobster eats shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227249#post1227249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Customer: \u201cWell, can\u2019t you put the part of dinner that is not from the sea on a plate by itself and sell it to me?\u201d<br /> Chef: \u201cOur lobster is amazing. You won\u2019t even know what to do with the steak if the lobster is not on the plate with it.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak. You already have steaks and plates right?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cIt would take too much time for the expediter to arrange the filet properly on a plate without the lobster to balance it out.\u201d<br /> Customer: \u201cI just want a steak, seafood is expensive. Can\u2019t I just pay for what I am going to eat?\u201d<br /> Waiter: \u201cYou heard the chef. You wouldn\u2019t even know what to do with the filet without the lobster.\u201d<br /> Customer:\u201dCan I just get a yes or no answer to my question?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this ignores who you're asking. If you asked the other customers why they have surf and turf on the menu but not steak and if you could just get a meal without bottom feeders in it, it would be pretty normal for them, rather than a simple yes or no, you got a lot of reasons why the restaurant might offer surf and turf but not offer steak by itself, and to ask (again) that you stop calling lobster bottom-feeders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T17:57:57-07:00","id":1227288,"title":"","content":"@satchel: I have not at any time accused anyone of being a liar. The 85% figure was derived from some quick math based on Secrets of the covenants and one of the 1e clanbooks. I did a quick page count and divided. They matched pretty closely. For other books, I would have to page through them to find out the ratios. I never said 85% of all the books were fluff and 15% crunch. I used the example of what are in my opinion, the worse offenders. As to your last statement. I don't understand why the idea of different products being published would be offensive. Why would it be more or less offensive that certain customers want to purchase some of your products but not all of your products. <br /> <br /> Regardless, I do understand the viewpoint and argument that setting/lore cannot be separated from mechanics because the two are one and the same. I don't agree with this viewpoint though. And it seems that Onyx Path doesn't either. Behold! <b><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness: God-Machine Rules Update</a> </b>I should have referenced this from the start, but I had forgotten about it. They gave it away free and are still doing so. I would have happily paid for it. I would love to see such books released for all the game lines, and am willing to pay for them.<br /> <br /> Regarding supplements: If the trend continues wherein the new merits/devotions etc are all grouped in the appendix sections, then perhaps we could have a compendium of all the appendixes from various supplements in one place. Which, again, I would gladly pay money for. Alternatively, the appendices could be sold individually as a pamphlet for a discount so that we wouldn't have to wait 5-10 years for a compendium. <br /> <br /> \u200b/sarcasm: However, the word appendix does have a connotation of being unnecessary or an afterthought. Perhaps we should use a less offensive word for it. /sarcasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T18:19:53-07:00","id":1227294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227288#post1227288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b/sarcasm: However, the word appendix does have a connotation of being unnecessary or an afterthought. Perhaps we should use a less offensive word for it. /sarcasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The definition of appendix is <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1.a tube-shaped sac attached to and opening into the lower end of the large intestine in humans and some other mammals.<br /> <b>2. a section or table of additional matter at the end of a book or document.</b> </div> </div> </div>The definition of fluff is<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>noun</i><br /> 1.soft fibers from fabrics such as wool or cotton that accumulate in small light clumps.<br /> <b>2.entertainment or <u>writing</u> perceived as trivial or superficial.</b><br /> <br /> <i>verb</i><br /> 1.make (something) appear fuller and softer, typically by shaking or brushing it.<br /> <b>2.fail to perform or accomplish (something) successfully or well (used especially in a sporting or acting context).</b> </div> </div> </div>The appendix is the section at the end, not an afterthought. I think one Frank Herbert and one JRR Tolkien would be quite cross if you assumed their appendices to be afterthoughts. Meanwhile, fluff is literally defined as a trivial piece of writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T18:23:09-07:00","id":1227295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227288#post1227288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@satchel: I have not at any time accused anyone of being a liar.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you use an analogy where you liken the process of publishing a book with much of the material stripped out to the much less involved process of a restaurant putting only one of two components of their entr\u00e9e on a plate, you are implying that the explanation of &quot;in this textual medium where the mechanics reference specific fictional constructs that we describe outside of the framing of the dice mechanics, taking the dice mechanics in isolation is functionally detrimental to reader understanding&quot; is unsatisfactory just because you don't care for nonspecific varieties of those types of extramechanical description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to your last statement. I don't understand why the idea of different products being published would be offensive. Why would it be more or less offensive that certain customers want to purchase some of your products but not all of your products. </div> </div> </div>&quot;More inoffensive&quot; here means &quot;something people would have less of a problem with.&quot; You could stand to angle more of your pitch to that standard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would have happily paid for it. I would love to see such books released for all the game lines, and am willing to pay for them. </div> </div> </div>The Rules Update exists, has existed, and will continue to exist as a block of text that was created and published in the format in which you can find it now. It was created as an addition to the New World Of Darkness Core Rulebook at a time when an officially-termed &quot;new edition&quot; was not in the cards, as a stopgap measure to inform the systems that would go on to be known as the Chronicles of Darkness and its various Second Edition gamelines.<br /> <br /> To get the same thing out of, say, VtR2e Core, you would have to comb through most of the middle of the book, pare down descriptive text, figure out what if any changes in layout and order of information needed making, and possibly write appropriate summaries to bridge gaps in the content to make this work as an official product.<br /> <br /> For contrast, if you have the books on PDF then making a set of printouts to use for quick-reference is the work of <i>maybe</i> an afternoon or two per book.<br /> <br /> You still haven't actually answered the question: what is the chicken in this analogy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T18:29:16-07:00","id":1227298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227295#post1227295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You still haven't actually answered the question: what is the chicken in this analogy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to know the answer to this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T18:45:29-07:00","id":1227308,"title":"","content":"@Charlaquin: I didn't do an exhaustive analysis of every book's crunch to fluff ratio. However, it seems pedantic to me to keep quibbling over this. However, if it will satisfy you:<br /> <br /> Clanbook Daeva: 10%<br /> Clanbook Gangrel: 13%<br /> Clanbook Mekhet: 33%<br /> Clanbook Nosferatu: 16%<br /> Clanbook Ventrue: 17%<br /> Secrets of the Covenants: 12%<br /> Average: 17% (figures have been rounded)<br /> <br /> The point is, there is definitely a dichotomy which exists. One side of the dichotomy is definitely a minority of the page count. I think the imbalance is much greater and the dividing line much easier to see in the game supplements than in the core books, but it does exist and the dichotomy can be separated.<br /> <br /> I asked the other customers their opinions because thought perhaps other customers would feel as I do and make their opinions known<br /> <br /> And lobsters <i>are</i> bottom feeders. Fact.<br /> <br /> @satchel: I'm not sure what the exact metaphor is anymore. After I quoted part of it, it was edited by ArcaneArts. I do think that I have made my point quite clear though, and been pretty clear about what I am asking for.<br /> <br /> For the most part, I feel what I have been getting in return is pedantics and pearl clutching. Come on... We all know the difference between fluff/setting and crunch/mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 06-13-2018, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T18:54:36-07:00","id":1227309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227308#post1227308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin: I didn't do an exhaustive analysis of every book's crunch to fluff ratio. However, it seems pedantic to me to keep quibbling over this. However, if it will satisfy you:<br /> <br /> Clanbook Daeva: 10%<br /> Clanbook Gangrel: 13%<br /> Clanbook Mekhet: 33%<br /> Clanbook Nosferatu: 16%<br /> Clanbook Ventrue: 17%<br /> Secrets of the Covenants: 12%<br /> Average: 17% (figures have been rounded)<br /> <br /> The point is, there is definitely a dichotomy which exists. One side of the dichotomy is definitely a minority of the page count. I think the imbalance is much greater and the dividing line much easier to see in the game supplements than in the core books, but it does exist and the dichotomy can be separated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that by word count or by page number? I ask because the layout of the lore in Secrets of the Covenant means that there are fewer words per page. The same would be true for the clan books since they are written in the same still. I recall it being mentioned when SotC came out that each chapter had the same word count since I made the mistake of counting the pages when someone asked what the ratios were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T19:00:22-07:00","id":1227311,"title":"","content":"I didn't count the words in SotC, but if the chapters have the same amount, then it should be 17% for SotC. and again, I wish I could have bought the appendix separately, but I did buy the whole book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T19:02:58-07:00","id":1227312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227288#post1227288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b/sarcasm: However, the word appendix does have a connotation of being unnecessary or an afterthought. Perhaps we should use a less offensive word for it. /sarcasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you could stop making fun of people for taking issue with the words you use, that'd be great. I'm using black text right now, please don't make me use red text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T19:05:57-07:00","id":1227313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227308#post1227308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@satchel: I'm not sure what the exact metaphor is anymore. After I quoted part of it, it was edited by ArcaneArts. I do think that I have made my point quite clear though, and been pretty clear about what I am asking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The edit is still in the post you responded with, but why not-we (incorrectly) switched the mechanics over to being the seasoning/sides/drink and the setting over to the steak, at which point you said &quot;yay, let's trade out the steak for chicken.&quot;<br /> <br /> So running with that, if the steak is the current fluff, what is the chicken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-13-2018, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T19:36:18-07:00","id":1227322,"title":"","content":"The chicken would be other fluff. IE: other settings. I know nothing prevents me from taking the rules of Onyx Path products and using them in any game setting I see fit. I'm just asking for the option to purchase them separately so I would not have to pay a steak I will not eat. Perhaps we should avoid metaphors going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T20:09:03-07:00","id":1227330,"title":"","content":"figurehead's able to have a negative view of certain aspects of the game, they didn't seem to come here with a 'Change My Mind' sign as much as a 'I Want This,' and it doesn't really matter what others or myself think about it. People have asked for more outre things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T20:16:09-07:00","id":1227331,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the metaphors aren\u2019t really helping anyone. Much more efficient to just talk about what we\u2019re actually talking about.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019ve never really understood the desire to use a set of mechanics designed for a particular setting to play a different setting. The point of the mechanics is to give you tools to interact with the setting. And I\u2019m a proponent of using the right tools for the job you\u2019re doing. I wouldn\u2019t want to use the d20 system to play a political intrigue game starring vampires, and I wouldn\u2019t use the Requiem rules to play a high fantasy game about recovering treasure from subterranean complexes.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a line that must be drawn at some point of what non-mechanical content you consider fluff vs. crunch. To use a simple example, look at the first Merit that appears in the so-called crunch section of Secrets of the Covenants; alley cat. The purely mechanical function of that Merit is to decrease the total number of 8s, 9s, or 10s that need to be rolled in order to achieve critical success on certain rolls by the dot rating. Are the rolls it applies to part of the crunch? I think most people would say yes - the mechanics are incomplete without them after all. But, \u201crolling to hide, evade, or pursue\u201d is not game-mechanical information. It necessarily references what is happening in the fiction, not a value on the character sheet. How about the fact that it only applies \u201cin your character\u2019s home city streets\u201d? That qualifier is meaningless without reference to the setting, and in fact suggests an urban, probably modern, setting. How about the fact that the Merit requires a dot of Carthian Status? That\u2019s a much more direct reference to the mechanics, and yet says even more about the setting - you can\u2019t know what that means without knowing what a Carthian is. And then we get to the description of Carthians being the vampires most intimately familiar with city streets. Indisputably setting content, yet it takes up half of the text of the Merit, and also contextualizes the mechanics of the Merit.<br /> <br /> And this is just one very simple Merit. The line between game mechanics and setting content only gets blurrier with more complex mechanics like Conditions, or Disciplines. The rules are intimately connected with the stories they are used to tell, such that the categories of \u201cfluff\u201d and \u201ccrunch\u201d are ultimately arbitrary. You can point to parts of the books that do not contain mechanics text and say \u201cI want less of this kind of content\u201d easily enough, but it\u2019s much harder to separate the setting content from the rules content on the parts that do contain mechanical text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T20:41:37-07:00","id":1227336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227330#post1227330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">figurehead's able to have a negative view of certain aspects of the game, they didn't seem to come here with a 'Change My Mind' sign as much as a 'I Want This,' and it doesn't really matter what others or myself think about it. People have asked for more outre things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but there's nothing any of us can do to give it to them, so what other avenues for discussion are available here beyond reasons someone might or might not want it and reasons OPP might or might not offer it? Again, this is the customer asking other customers why the service provider doesn't offer the specific service they want. The <i>best</i> we can do is offer educated guesses as to why that might not be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T20:42:16-07:00","id":1227337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227308#post1227308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come on... We all know the difference between fluff/setting and crunch/mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>really fucking don't</i>, is the thing, at least not in the baffling framework you're using where the crown jewel of your argument is that a set of books specifically conceived of as collections of in-universe documents and a category of book that has the words &quot;fiction anthology&quot; specifically contained in its titles are what you want less of and this somehow has anything to do with the volume of text in any other book where there isn't an immediately-discernible divide between &quot;this is part of the game-fiction&quot; and &quot;this is the stuff that involves your character sheets.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227322#post1227322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chicken would be other fluff. IE: other settings. I know nothing prevents me from taking the rules of Onyx Path products and using them in any game setting I see fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there is the problem: This is asking for a Chronicles of Darkness Without Chronicles Of Darkness book. This is asking for the Revised Storytelling System SRD, which is, again, <i>a different thing entirely</i> from &quot;what if OPP made mechanics anthologies?&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's a reasonable thing to want for gaming purposes, but it is <i>maybe not the best use of your time</i> to ask other people who do not have any sway in the publishing process about this in a weird discount-oriented hypothetical based around false equivalence and vague I-know-it-when-I-see-it definition of terms for a framing that is specifically about <i>removing</i> content from a block of text.<br /> <br /> Like, would you do this to the engine for a video game you didn't like the story or aesthetics for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T21:09:25-07:00","id":1227344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227336#post1227336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Again, this is the customer asking other customers why the service provider doesn't offer the specific service they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>There may be a misconception. This is actually a customer asking other customers if they would be interested in a product that is not currently on offer in the hopes that they would say yes. If enough said yes, perhaps the company would see the demand and make with the supply.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, my original post was not received in the straight forward manner in which I intended it, and my not perfect memory didn't think of things that I hadn't thought of for years. With that in mind, my original post should have gone like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1227343-product-request\"><b>Product Request</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T00:02:42-07:00","id":1227376,"title":"","content":"From my perspective:<br /> <br /> Isn't the Chronicles of Darkness gameline known for putting role-playing first instead of roll-playing? And thus asking for more mechanics over setting and lore is being disingenuous to the entire gameline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 06-14-2018, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T01:30:08-07:00","id":1227389,"title":"","content":"1. I don't think it's true to say CoD is more known for 'role playing' over 'roll playing.' Onyx Path does not have a monopoly on that. Further, I seem to recall a lot of emphasis on toolkit/sandbox style books as way to differentiate it from the metaplot heavy Classic WoD. I also don't think liking the dice mechanics means you can infer the quality of play at someone's table.<br /> <br /> 2. I have not asked for more mechanics over setting. I have asked for existing mechanics to be released separately. <br /> <br /> 3. I do not think it is disingenuous to ask for a product. This thread was a sincere request.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T02:00:29-07:00","id":1227391,"title":"","content":"For me the games sometimes feel a bit too &quot;crunchy&quot;. Makes me think &quot;how can I do this within the rules&quot; instead of just doing it. For instance I get what social manouvering was meant to accomplish but it feels a tad artificial for me. I'm not trying to discuss the game mechanics per se just to note that people have a different preference about the scale of crunchyness- fluffyness. And each game catters to a different audience, perhaps people who play OP games are more on the fluff side.In which case printing a &quot;Rules compendium&quot; wouldn't be economically sound.<br /> <br /> Also I like the term &quot;Fluff&quot;, make me think about something that's pleasant to touch and deal with and games are meant to bring a sense of pleasure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T04:44:17-07:00","id":1227406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227376#post1227376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my perspective:<br /> <br /> Isn't the Chronicles of Darkness gameline known for putting role-playing first instead of roll-playing? And thus asking for more mechanics over setting and lore is being disingenuous to the entire gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>This paradox has really vexed me. The Onyx Path seems to think that, but they also write extremely crunch heavy books for such an approach (clanbooks/SotC aside). I get why (it's part of the &quot;crunch informs setting&quot; idea) but it makes me less interested in writing my own experiences here on this forum because they definitely fall outside the intended scopes of the games (most would consider us powergaming) while also being fully supported by the mechanics of most gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T07:21:47-07:00","id":1227430,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think Onyx Path does focus on \u201crole play over roll play\u201d (*hurk*). <i>White Wolf</i> made its brand on being \u201cthe role player\u2019s RPG\u201d in a time when D&amp;D 3e was the industry standard. And like the witticism about not having to outrun the bear, White Wolf didn\u2019t need the lightest mechanics on the market to sell itself that way, only to be light<i>er</i> than D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path has inherited that reputation for being \u201cthe story gamer\u2019s alternative to D&amp;D,\u201d but it hasn\u2019t really been their MO for a long time. They\u2019ve long since carved out their niche, and mechanics-light is not what that niche is. And I\u2019m pretty sure they\u2019re well aware of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T10:25:30-07:00","id":1227465,"title":"","content":"What does (*hurk*) mean?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 06-14-2018, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T10:43:30-07:00","id":1227467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227465#post1227465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does (*hurk*) mean?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to speak for Willow, but I believe it is about the idea that a number of people share that that supposed dichotomy (roll-play vs role-play) is spurious and non-helpful. It contains both a division of the games that is unneeded and not designed to be there (see this whole thread) and carries the connotations that 'role-play' is superior in that real RPGers care more about the acting than the dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:13:49-07:00","id":1227472,"title":"","content":"Thanks for responding. I understood the content of her post via context. What I'm asking is what does (*hurk*) mean by itself? Is it supposed to be gagging/dry heaving/vomiting sounds? That's my best guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:18:50-07:00","id":1227475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227465#post1227465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does (*hurk*) mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s the sound of throwing up in one\u2019s own mouth a little bit. I make it when I use certain expressions that are common in RPG discussions to express my distaste for them. Role play vs. roll play is one of them, and ElvesofZion gave a pretty good summary of why I so detest that phrase. Another one is \u201cgood roleplaying.\u201d As in, \u201cI like to award bonus experience for good roleplaying.\u201d These idioms and others like them present a warped view of roleplaying and roleplaying games, which I feel are harmful to the hobby. But, they are so ubiquitous in RPG discussion that it is sometimes more convenient, or even necessary, to use them to quickly communicate my point. So I use an onamonapia to express that, though I am using the idiom in question for expediency\u2019s sake, I feel a little bit gross for doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:20:08-07:00","id":1227476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227472#post1227472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for responding. I understood the content of her post via context. What I'm asking is what does (*hurk*) mean by itself? Is it supposed to be gagging/dry heaving/vomiting sounds? That's my best guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re correct, that was my intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:09:16-07:00","id":1227488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1227467#post1227467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to speak for Willow, but I believe it is about the idea that a number of people share that that supposed dichotomy (roll-play vs role-play) is spurious and non-helpful. It contains both a division of the games that is unneeded and not designed to be there (see this whole thread) and carries the connotations that 'role-play' is superior in that real RPGers care more about the acting than the dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. If anything, I\u2019d say OPP\u2019s current design approach is to try and deliberately blur that line (in as much as it really exists in the first place) as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:46:54-07:00","id":1227497,"title":"","content":"People tend to conflate roleplaying with acting. That\u2019s the root of most things that I say *hurk* about. In my opinion, roleplaying is the act of imagining yourself as someone else and/or in a situation, and making decisions as you think you or that other person would do in that situation. Rolling dice is not the opposite of roleplaying, it\u2019s a tool that facilitates roleplaying by acting as a neutral arbiter to fairly resolve uncertainties that arise in the imagined scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:13:18-07:00","id":1227519,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I over explained then since the onamonapia itself was the actual intent of the question.<br /> <br /> It's just that it is an often sore subject for myself like it is for Willow and I think is relevant to the thread as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a> pointed out. Onyx Path has not been going for 'rules light' but for integrated mechanics that exist to facilitate the game the way Willow then said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T17:34:06-07:00","id":1228425,"title":"","content":"My two cents - the Chronicle of Darkness books aren't good reference documents. They aren't the worst (classic White Wolf, I'm looking at <i>you</i>), but they have a variety of layout decisions that makes it harder to actually find things. This a general thing in the industry, not a specific thing - layout and organization are <i>complicated</i>. Having the rule toys all cleanly laid out would be a <i>great</i> help.<br /> <br /> I would, however, support them making a little &quot;core rules&quot; pdf that has stuff like Social Maneuvering and the ephemeral being rules. Then maybe they could stop reprinting them all the time, taking up valuable word-count (if that actually <i>does</i> take up word-count - I'm not privy to such things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T23:02:06-07:00","id":1228507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1228425#post1228425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would, however, support them making a little &quot;core rules&quot; pdf that has stuff like Social Maneuvering and the ephemeral being rules. Then maybe they could stop reprinting them all the time, taking up valuable word-count (if that actually <i>does</i> take up word-count - I'm not privy to such things).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that was sort of the intent of the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook, though they seem dead set on reprinting those rules (with missing bits leading to questions like whether vampires regain wilpower through sleep) with every single gameline despite how much page space they could spend on other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T02:56:30-07:00","id":1228538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1226884-more-crunch-less-fluff-please?p=1228507#post1228507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that was sort of the intent of the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook, though they seem dead set on reprinting those rules (with missing bits leading to questions like whether vampires regain wilpower through sleep) with every single gameline despite how much page space they could spend on other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the intent with the original World of Darkness rulebook. They specifically didn't want to do it with second edition. The Chronicles of Darkness rulebook contains rules for playing games with human characters. Systems like social maneuvering and ephemeral entities are collected in that book for people who wish to play a Chronicles of Darkness (gameline, not setting) game rather than being intended to use with other games in the franchise. The reprinted systems are there in other gamelines because they're intended to work standalone, unlike first edition.<br /> <br /> Also, claryifying if anyone hasn't been up to date with the various discussions in other threads, the reason WP gain from sleep is missing in some books is because Vampire was the first second edition core rule book (rather than just containing an appendix like GMC or DTD) and thus is the copypasta template for all other 2e core books. Only vampires were intended to not gain WP through sleep. If that rule is missing from other games it's because they accidentally didn't reintroduce that rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}